                    "gaia_arp_motif_616": {
                      "_children": {
                        "Core": {
                          "name": "arp_motif",
                          "tooltip": "How held keys are assigned when the chord has more notes than the pattern. Keep low (L): retain the lowest key across repetitions. Keep low+high (L&H): retain both extremes. No fixed note (_): rotate without retaining either extreme. Up/down describes the direction of this rotation, not a new note pattern. Phrase uses the last-played key to transpose the phrase.\nThese performance controls send live; only note blocks and END STEP use Send Pattern.\nHardware codes: UP/L = Up · keep low; UP/L&H = Up · keep low+high; UP/_ = Up · no fixed note; DOWN/L = Down · keep low; DOWN/L&H = Down · keep low+high; DOWN/_ = Down · no fixed note; UP&DOWN/L = Up/down · keep low; UP&DOWN/L&H = Up/down · keep low+high; UP&DOWN/_ = Up/down · no fixed note; RANDOM/L = Random · keep low; RANDOM/_ = Random · no fixed note; PHRASE = Phrase · last key",
                          "id": "gaia_arp_motif_616",
                          "description": "Arpeggio Motif — 10 00 0C 02",
                          "controlType": "Combobox"
                        },
                        "Transform": {
